<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n76280" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψ</span></b>  (A), ἡ, poetic
		Noun, used in obliq. cases of sg., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπός, ὀπί,
			ὄπα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>voice</i>, whether in speaking, shouting, lamenting, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀτρείδεω ὀπὸς ἔκλυον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					16.76
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				14.150
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18.222
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				22.451
			</span></i>, etc.; or in singing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κίρκης . . ἀειδούσης ὀπὶ καλῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					10.221
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				5.61
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄειδον ἀμειβόμεναι ὀπὶ καλῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.604
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				41
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				7.84
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				B.
				16.129
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				60
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc.; also of cicadae, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄπα λειριόεσσαν ἱεῖσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					3.152
				</span></i>
			; of lambs, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκούουσαι ὄπα ἀρνῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					4.435
				</span></i>
			; of flutes, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐλῶν φθεγγομένων ἱμερόεσσαν ὄπα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					532
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>word</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς γὰρ ἐγὼν ὄπ᾽ ἄκουσα θεῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					7.53
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμείλικτον δ᾽ ὄπ᾽ ἄκουσαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					11.137
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				21.98
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				1068
			</span></i> (lyr.), etc. (Cogn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπος,
				εἰπεῖν</span>.)</div>
